      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports circadian rhythm disruption under constant light/artificial lighting, but it does not define circadian rhythm itself as “the body’s biological pattern” or explicitly state that it follows the daily light–dark cycle.",
        "The balance and melatonin claims are drawn from a young rat model; the definition generalizes those findings beyond the studied animals and beyond the specific experimental context.",
        "“Modern lighting conditions” is broader than the packet’s wording and is not directly established as a general cause in the supplied source."
